# ppcrlwimiwidth Honest Null-Medium Leg & Vacuity-Floor Clause (c) Report

The vacuity-floor clause (c) breach identified in `regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth/killtable_20260911/mutate_rlwimi.py:179` has been repaired in-round. The previous `NULL_MEDIUM` leg recompiled `FIXED_BLOCK` byte-identical to `BASE` and `RESTORED`, falsely reporting 28/28 because it was an unmutated duplicate of the base leg under a misleading label.

The real null medium—an honest identity body in `X(rlwimi)` that decodes and retires the instruction with zero insertion into the destination register—was built and measured in scratch clone `/tmp/gxrlwimi_clone`. Zero files in `build/`, `build-asan/`, `/tmp/gxsec-build`, or `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` were touched.

