## 1. Identity Body Implementation

In [mutate_rlwimi.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/ppcrlwimiwidth/killtable_nullmedium_20260911/mutate_rlwimi.py), the body of `X(rlwimi)` in `src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c` was replaced with:

```c
X(rlwimi)
{
	/*  NULL MEDIUM: decode and retire, insert nothing.  */
	MODE_uint_t ra = reg(ic->arg[1]);
	uint32_t iword = ic->arg[2];
	int rc = iword & 1;

	reg(ic->arg[1]) = ra;
	if (rc)
		update_cr0(cpu, ra);
}
```

### Engineering Rationale:
1. **Zero Insertion / Pure Identity**: `ra` is loaded from `reg(ic->arg[1])` and written back unmodified via `reg(ic->arg[1]) = ra;`. No bits from `rS` (`ic->arg[0]`) are rotated, masked, or inserted.
2. **Preservation of `rc` / `update_cr0` Axis**: `rc = iword & 1` and `if (rc) update_cr0(cpu, ra);` are kept so the Condition Register CR0 recording axis remains active, isolating the measurement strictly to the data-insertion axis.
3. **Clean Warning-Free Build**: `ra`, `iword`, `rc`, `cpu`, and `ic` are all used, producing zero compiler warnings under `-Wall -Werror`.

